// The dogfood app's own program — and the whole of an abide app's config: extend what abide ships,
// name what to check. The seams are in `package.json`'s `imports`, so there is nothing about `#ui` or
// `#server` here and nothing to keep in step between two files.
//
// The type fixtures under `tests/types/invalid` are SUPPOSED to fail. They are checked deliberately,
// through their own config, by a case that asserts the diagnostics — and a repo whose own typecheck
// is red says nothing at all, so they are not part of this one. A pattern rather than the one path,
// because they are in two trees: the `.abide` sources and what they compiled to under `.abide/types`.
{
    "extends": "abide/tsconfig.json",
    "include": ["**/*.ts", ".abide/types/**/*.ts"],
    "exclude": ["**/types/invalid"]
}
